2026-11-10 07:46:15,179 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Investigation Questions — Findings
2026-11-10 07:46:15,179 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q1 — Andrews-1 (benign file sharing?):** The printer share `\\ANDREWS-1\HPLaserJ` confirms Andrews-1 is a known network host. However, **5 separate drive mappings** (A:, C:, D:, E:, F:) go far beyond printer or casual sharing. Finding **f_5ed43b6d updated** to document all 5 drives and the printer share, with explicit acknowledgment of the alternative explanation and why it is not dispositive.
2026-11-10 07:46:15,181 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q2 — Cain/PWDump3 execution evidence:** Prefetch `CAIN.EXE-23D61279.pf` shows **run count = 2, last run 2004-08-27 15:33:03** — Cain was definitely executed. PWDump3 has only the zip archive; **no prefetch confirms execution**. Finding **f_a0f4c775 updated** to document both facts clearly.
2026-11-10 07:46:15,181 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q3 — Cerberus reports (self-scanning?):** 172.16.0.0/24 is RFC 1918 space consistent with home/lab or VPN target. The completed multi-protocol scan reports for 172.16.0.2 demonstrate operational tool use. The alternative (self-scanning a home lab) is acknowledged in the finding's existing description; no change to severity or confidence warranted — the scan reports exist regardless.
2026-11-10 07:46:15,182 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q4 — samdump.dll YARA hit (false positive?):** The YARA rule fires on the string `$g: samdump.dll` — a name-based match, not a binary code signature. This is consistent with Cain's known bundled samdump.dll component in `C:\Program Files\Cain\`. Finding **f_a0f4c775 updated** to clarify the detection mechanism and explain why the corroborating Cain evidence removes the false-positive risk.
2026-11-10 07:46:15,183 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q5 — rpcapd (ever started?):** Registry confirms `Start = Manual` — not auto-start. However, `DAEMON_MGM.EXE` (the service manager) shows **run count = 3** in prefetch, indicating active management beyond mere installation. Finding **f_5e755250 updated** with both facts; "inference" confidence retained as correct.
2026-11-10 07:46:15,185 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q6 — Ethereal captures with third-party traffic:** [NEGATIVE] Search of full tsk.filelist found **zero .pcap/.cap/.eth files**. No saved capture sessions exist. New finding **f_30f281e7 submitted**.
2026-11-10 07:46:15,186 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q7 — NetBus.bad (AV quarantine?):** [NEGATIVE] Complete review of registry.system services found **no antivirus software installed** on the machine. The McAfee `.bad` quarantine alternative is impossible. New finding **f_0a5a69ba submitted** explicitly ruling out the AV quarantine hypothesis.
2026-11-10 07:46:15,188 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q8 — Forensic collection misclassification:** Searched for FTK, EnCase, Helix, COFEE, Guidance, IR tool signatures. **None found.** This system is an evidence subject, not a collection platform.
2026-11-10 07:46:15,189 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q9 — MACE timestamp consistency:** File timestamps reflect original tool release dates (1998–2004) preserved in archive extraction — consistent with downloading and unpacking tool collections. No evidence of timestomping identified.
2026-11-10 07:46:15,189 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q10 — Security student vs. attacker:** While organized directories could theoretically reflect study material, the totality of evidence — `mrevilrulez` IRC identity, #Elite.Hackers channel membership, completed operational scan reports, Cain run twice, Anonymizer in use — is inconsistent with passive study. The security-student alternative is not supported.
2026-11-10 07:46:15,190 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q11 — NetStumbler/wardriving (legitimate IT survey?):** While wireless site surveys can be legitimate, the combination with Ethereal/WinPcap for capture, Anonymizer for OPSEC, and no business-context artifacts points strongly away from legitimate IT work.
2026-11-10 07:46:15,191 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Quality Audit Results
